# 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior Flutter engineer, mobile UI/UX designer, database architect, financial software developer, cybersecurity engineer, and quality assurance specialist.

Build a complete, production-ready mobile application named **My Daily Khata – Expense Tracker**.

The app must enable individuals and families to record everyday income and expenditure, manage household budgets, track savings, review payment methods, monitor spending patterns, and generate accurate financial reports.

Deliver functional source code, a working application, persistent storage, automated tests, and build instructions.

Do not deliver only a prototype, static dashboard, or non-functional UI.

## 1.1 Mandatory currency policy

Use Indian Rupees exclusively throughout the application.

- Currency code: `INR`
- Currency symbol: `₹`
- Locale for monetary formatting: `en_IN`
- Number grouping: Indian lakh/crore grouping
- Date format: `dd-MM-yyyy`
- Time format: 12-hour or 24-hour, according to user preference
- Currency selection: Disabled; INR is permanently fixed

Examples:

| Numeric value | Required display |
|---:|---:|
| 50 | ₹50.00 |
| 500 | ₹500.00 |
| 12500 | ₹12,500.00 |
| 125000 | ₹1,25,000.00 |
| 1234567 | ₹12,34,567.00 |
| 123456789 | ₹12,34,56,789.00 |

On compact dashboard cards, insignificant decimal places may be omitted: for example, ₹1,25,000. Never sacrifice Indian grouping.

Never show USD, $, EUR, or any foreign currency in monetary fields, charts, reports, notifications, exports, receipts, or sample data.

Use the English locale for numeric currency formatting in both English and Odia language modes. Translate labels and descriptions into the selected language.

